<logo type="word"><image src="/lib/ruby/gems/4.0.0/gems/metanorma-ogc-2.10.0/lib/isodoc/ogc/html/Logos_2026/1_Blue_Logos/OGC-new-logo.png" mimetype="image/png"/></logo>
</organization></contributor><edition language="">1.0</edition><edition language="en">edition 1.0</edition><version>1.0</version><language current="true">en</language><script current="true">Latn</script><abstract><p>GeoSPARQL provides a standard framework for storing, querying and representing geospatial information using RDF and SPARQL. Although GeoSPARQL 1.1 has some support for 3D geometries, its current vocabulary, geometry representations, and query functions provide limited support for 3D spatial data and functions. At the same time, the use of 3D spatial data is increasing across domains such as geospatial information, Building Information Modelling (BIM), construction, infrastructure, emergency response, cultural heritage, and computer graphics.</p>

<p>This white paper investigates the requirements and opportunities for extending GeoSPARQL with improved 3D capabilities. It examines the current capabilities and limitations of GeoSPARQL 1.1, reviews related standards, data formats ontologies, and analyses use cases gathered from different domains. Particular attention is given to the representation and querying of 3D geometries and topology, semantic decomposition of complex 3D objects, interoperability with existing 3D standards, and functions in three-dimensional environments.</p>

<p>The paper evaluates potential extensions according to their relevance, benefits, and technical feasibility. The objective is not to replace existing 3D modelling or geometry standards, but to investigate how GeoSPARQL can provide a common semantic and spatial query layer over heterogeneous 3D data. Such capabilities could enable machine-readable and interoperable 3D spatial analysis without requiring data from different domains to be converted into a single homogeneous representation. Potential benefits include improved integration of GIS, BIM, and other 3D data sources; spatial and semantic querying of complex 3D objects; 3D topology and connectivity analysis; route and accessibility analysis; and applications in construction, safety, emergency response, and other domains involving three-dimensional environments.</p>
</abstract><status><stage language="">draft</stage><stage language="en">Draft</stage></status><copyright><from>2026</from><owner><organization>
<name>Open Geospatial Consortium</name>
<abbreviation>OGC</abbreviation></organization></owner></copyright><keyword><vocab>OGC;  GeoSPARQL; 3D; 3D geospatial data; 3D BIM; semantic 3D modelling; 3D spatial querying; 3D geometry; 3D topology; RDF; SPARQL; BIM; IFC; CityGML; semantic interoperability; 3D routing;</vocab></keyword><ext><doctype>technical-paper</doctype><flavor>ogc</flavor><stage>draft</stage></ext></bibdata><localized-strings><localized-string key="scope" language="en">Scope</localized-string><localized-string key="symbolsabbrev" language="en">Symbols and abbreviated terms</localized-string><localized-string key="abbrev" language="en">Abbreviated terms</localized-string><localized-string key="symbols" language="en">Symbols</localized-string><localized-string key="table_of_contents" language="en">Contents</localized-string><localized-string key="introduction" language="en">Introduction</localized-string><localized-string key="foreword" language="en">Preface</localized-string><localized-string key="abstract" language="en">Abstract</localized-string><localized-string key="acknowledgements" language="en">Acknowledgements</localized-string><localized-string key="executivesummary" language="en">Executive summary</localized-string><localized-string key="termsdef" language="en">Terms and definitions</localized-string><localized-string key="termsdefsymbolsabbrev" language="en">Terms, definitions, symbols and abbreviated terms</localized-string><localized-string key="termsdefsymbols" language="en">Terms, definitions and symbols</localized-string><localized-string key="termsdefabbrev" language="en">Terms, definitions and abbreviated terms</localized-string><localized-string key="normref" language="en">Normative references</localized-string><localized-string key="bibliography" language="en">Bibliography</localized-string><localized-string key="index" language="en">Index</localized-string><localized-string key="see" language="en">see</localized-string><localized-string key="see_also" language="en">see al