<p id="_5b74a675-e9be-c966-9e9f-5f610498140e" semx-id="_5b74a675-e9be-c966-9e9f-5f610498140e"><strong>Category</strong></p>

<p id="_254daf04-7a08-f1c3-8129-de5458a7b164" semx-id="_254daf04-7a08-f1c3-8129-de5458a7b164">Semantic improvement</p>

<p id="_d0e928f5-8836-4ce2-c6c9-99d82599f5b4" semx-id="_d0e928f5-8836-4ce2-c6c9-99d82599f5b4"><strong>Description</strong></p>

<p id="_acc3e753-573a-873e-1b06-0a51da767973" semx-id="_acc3e753-573a-873e-1b06-0a51da767973">GeoSPARQL 3D should be aligned to other vocabularies and standard which currently provide 3D support in different knowledge domains. Especially alignments to  <link target="https://technical.buildingsmart.org/standards/ifc/ifc-formats/ifcowl/" id="_aa4dc0a6-90fb-8c49-e618-7efce55305c0">ifcOWL</link><fmt-link target="https://technical.buildingsmart.org/standards/ifc/ifc-formats/ifcowl/">ifcOWL</fmt-link> and the <link target="https://www.web3d.org/x3d/content/semantics/semantics.html" id="_81c89fb0-3db6-e286-8cd6-19518a36c5de">X3D vocabulary</link><fmt-link target="https://www.web3d.org/x3d/content/semantics/semantics.html">X3D vocabulary</fmt-link> would position the GeoSPARQL vocabulary as a link between these different standards.</p>

<p id="_44708538-a3c2-0e40-f444-1ddb3ff1781a" semx-id="_44708538-a3c2-0e40-f444-1ddb3ff1781a"><strong>Related work</strong></p>

