<title id="_b51a74c9-9298-6f2f-1444-e9eb7dd03d2d" semx-id="_9eb31583-e999-3193-c827-594a202e0253">Boolean Geometry</title><fmt-title depth="2" id="_4199974c-8801-535b-03e8-fbf07bd56257"><span class="fmt-caption-label">B<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>5<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span></span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_b51a74c9-9298-6f2f-1444-e9eb7dd03d2d">Boolean Geometry</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Annex</span> B<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>5</fmt-xref-label>
<p id="_f00a846e-521f-9492-7d70-bd9d6ee72360" semx-id="_f00a846e-521f-9492-7d70-bd9d6ee72360">Defined constructively, not by its boundary. Boolean geometry is the representation of 3D shapes by combining or subtracting simpler solids using Boolean operations like union, intersection, and difference.</p>

